---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, COMPANY } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Legal notice" description="Company details for airworthywp.com and the Airworthy plugin.">
	<div class="wrap page-head">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1>Legal notice</h1>
	</div>
	<div class="wrap prose" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
		<p>This website and the Airworthy plugin are provided by:</p>
		<p>
			<strong>{ COMPANY.name }</strong><br />
			Registered in Ireland, company number { COMPANY.cro }<br />
			Registered office: { COMPANY.address }<br />
			VAT number: { COMPANY.vat }<br />
			Email: <a href={ `mailto:${ SITE.email.hello }` }>{ SITE.email.hello }</a><br />
			Website: <a href={ COMPANY.url }>{ COMPANY.url.replace( 'https://', '' ) }</a>
		</p>

		<h2>Licence</h2>
		<p>The Airworthy plugin is free software, released under the GNU General Public License. It bundles open-source libraries under their own licences; see the <a href="/docs/#bundled-libraries-and-licences">list in the docs</a>.</p>

		<h2>No warranty</h2>
		<p>Airworthy reads code without running it, so it can't catch every problem. Its results help you plan an upgrade; they're not a guarantee. Test on a staging copy of your site and keep a backup before changing your PHP version. As the licence says, the plugin comes without any warranty.</p>

		<h2>Trademarks</h2>
		<p>WordPress is a trademark of the WordPress Foundation. PHP is a trademark of the PHP Group. Airworthy is not affiliated with or endorsed by either. Plugin names mentioned on this site belong to their owners.</p>
	</div>
</Base>
